<section class="block-section story">
  <span class="section-tag">Story</span>
  <h2>What today is about</h2>
  <p class="sub">The signature U5 partner arrives today.</p>
  <p>Real stakeholders cite different evidence because they want different things. Today you map one stakeholder, then meet a partner that argues the other side at full strength, so you can practise answering it fairly.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Map what they want first, then their evidence.</strong> Use the 6 fields: Who They Are · What They Want · Evidence They Cite · Position · Power · Allies+Opponents. A Tamil Nadu delta farmer and a Karnataka upstream farmer read the same rainfall data differently because their <a class="key-term" href="/foundations/eal/u5/#interest" data-term="interest" aria-expanded="false"><strong>interest</strong></a> is different.</li>
    <li><strong>Meet <a href="/ai-partners/stakeholder-voice/">The Stakeholder Voice</a>.</strong> It plays the strongest version of any stakeholder you name, so you practise answering a strong argument, not a weak one. Your class's version is in the Interact card below.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This is the move your Position Paper's "Acknowledge competing concerns" section needs.</p>
</section>

